@startuml
' Phase 8 — Visualizer: as-built infrastructure. Copied from plan.uml and edited
' to the finished state at phase end.

title Phase 8 — Visualizer (as built)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "aa-visualizer (Go; imports contracts + memory)" as visualizer {
  component "visualizer (types + errors + clock)" as core
  component "source (EventSource seam + deterministic fake)" as source
  component "compat (observation metadata profile)" as compat
  component "session (event fold + identity mapping)" as session
  component "layout (pure deterministic layout + budget)" as layout
  component "replay (frames + time-travel cursor)" as replay
  component "bridge (live subscription -> same path)" as bridge
  component "browse (memory session browsing)" as browse
  component "retention (trail trimming)" as retention
}

package "aa-contracts (event taxonomy)" as contracts
package "aa-memory (query seam; used as-is)" as memory
package "aa-obsv (scaffolded; live transport deferred)" as obsv
package "aa-console (control-plane API, later)" as console
package "Wails + React/Three surface (deferred)" as ui

contracts --> core
core --> source
core --> compat
core --> session
compat --> session
core --> layout
session --> replay
layout --> replay
source --> bridge
replay --> bridge
session --> browse
replay --> browse
memory --> browse
replay --> retention
obsv ..> source : real Replay/Subscribe (deferred)
console ..> browse : control-plane API (later)
ui ..> replay : renders frames (deferred)

note right of source
  ADR-P8-001/002: consumes the shared
  contracts.Event taxonomy through a
  seam; events fold by Sequence, never
  the wall clock. A deterministic fake
  stands in for the deferred transport.
end note

note bottom of compat
  ADR-P8-004: secondary_paths and
  access_sequence are normalized by an
  explicit, versioned profile; unknown
  metadata is ignored and invalid
  supported values are rejected.
end note

note bottom of session
  ADR-P8-003: node identity derives
  from aggregate kind + id and is
  re-derived after replay, never
  persisted as truth.
end note

note bottom of layout
  ADR-P8-005/010: layout is a pure
  function of the graph with an
  explicit large-graph budget
  (250k nodes / 1M edges; 50k tested,
  100k benchmarked).
end note

note bottom of replay
  ADR-P8-007: one frame per event,
  built by the shared projection and
  layout path; the cursor snapshots,
  steps, and seeks into a fixed list.
end note

note bottom of bridge
  ADR-P8-006: a subscription is
  re-derived through replay.Build, so
  live frames equal replay frames.
end note

note bottom of browse
  ADR-P8-008: sessions are listed and
  loaded through the memory query seam
  (*query.Query). No explicit session
  id exists, so the key is payload
  sessionId, then ProjectID, then
  DefaultSessionID.
end note

note bottom of retention
  ADR-P8-009: retention trims the
  projected trail (replay frames),
  never the canonical source.
end note

@enduml
